  "theorem": {
    "name": "Hankel proportional-pencil tangent lemma",
    "proof_status": "algebraic identity plus machine replay",
    "statement": "For any field F, scalar c, syndrome vector v, and u=c v, the v9 Hankel pencil satisfies H(u)+Z H(v)=(c+Z)H(v). Thus every nonzero regular maximal minor has root set {-c}; every affine pivot slope with B_T nonzero is also -c; and B_T=0 implies A_T=0, hence contained.  After the tangent/common-code-line ledger removes Z=-c, the proportional branch contributes no aperiodic roots.",
